    "result_text": "The full suite is green \u2014 the only test is `AcceptanceTest`, and it passes along with a successful build.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `checkDigit` as a Luhn check digit computed over the digits of the owner's `customerCode`, returned on the owner representation.\n\nSince `checkDigit` is purely derived from the already-stored `customerCode`, I implemented it as a **read-time derived field** in the mapper \u2014 the same pattern the codebase already uses for `locality`, `identityKey`, and `contactPreference` \u2014 rather than adding an entity column or a POST-pipeline step. This guarantees it can never drift from the code it checks.\n\nChanges:\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `checkDigit` property (integer 0\u20139, `readOnly`) to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field.\n- **`OwnerCheckDigit.java`** (new) \u2014 a small single-source-of-truth helper with the standard Luhn algorithm (skips the hyphens in the code, doubles every second digit from the right, subtracting 9 on overflow, then rounds the sum up to the next multiple of ten).\n- **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 wired `checkDigit` via `@Mapping(..., qualifiedByName = \"checkDigit\")` and a `@Named` default delegating to the helper.\n\nThe acceptance test (`coreCheckDigitIsLuhnOfCustomerCode`), which recomputes Luhn from the returned `customerCode` and asserts the exact returned `checkDigit`, passes, and `BUILD SUCCESS` for the whole suite.",
